R-P5 R-UP7 R-SP16 R-SP24 R-DI1 R-EC12 R-PP4 (slice 036b2, the gap of slice 036b section 7): `probe.max` and the second search of a held move. Run 1 of `moves/hm1-noninteractive` with `[resolution] probe = { max = 2 }` in the root `talon.toml`: `add acme/json@2.2.0 --file ws/apps/b/main.roc` (member b has no json, member a holds 2.0.0). The first search has no tuple, and it starts no probe. The second search moves json to 2.2.0, and its loop starts one unit probe (json 2.2.0): the count is 1. The count goes on to the ladder (R-P5: one budget for the whole command). The ladder of member a needs the baseline (1 probe) and 3 unit probes (pf, lex, yaml). The budget has 2 and the loop used 1, so the baseline runs and no unit probe runs: exit 12, `the probe budget is spent: probe.max is 2 and 3 unit checks did not run.` (R-UP7, R-EC12). If the second search did not carry its count, the text would say 2 unit checks (one more unit probe would run).
